WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.440
Thanks for tuning in to Planetarian Daily, episode 69, coming to you on May 25th, 2026.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.500
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.600
A liver protein called HELLS2 shuts down production of the cholesterol carrier APOB.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.680
Researchers at UT Southwestern identified HELLS2 as the factor that suppresses transcription

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.200
of the APOB gene in hepatocytes.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:31.260
Reduced APOB production directly lowers the number of atherogenic particles released into circulation.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.560
The finding emerged from targeted genetic screens in human liver cells and mouse models.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.480
Mouse and cell culture data already show clear reductions in atherogenic particle output

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.300
when HELLS2 is active.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.620
Work continues to determine whether HELLS2 activity can be modulated therapeutically,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.400
because the protein acts at the gene expression level rather than on circulating lipotrines.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.980
It could complement existing statin or PCS canine therapies.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.760
Next steps include screening for small molecules that stabilize or activate the protein

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.060
without broad transcriptional side effects.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.060
Now, shifting to a very different area of research.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:19.020
McGill University scientists temporarily inhibited a pair of surface proteins on natural killer cells.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.100
The treated cells then penetrated the protective barriers erected by leukemia,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.640
glioblastoma, kidney cancer, and triple negative breast cancer cells.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.120
Laboratory tests showed markedly higher killing efficiency against these hard-to-treat lines.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.480
The approach is now being prepared for further pre-clinical evaluation.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.560
On a different note, older adults who drank concentrated nitrate-rich beetroot juice

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.940
twice daily for two weeks showed measurable reductions in blood pressure.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.680
The same regimen produced no comparable change in younger participants.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.980
The effect coincided with shifts in the composition of bacteria living in the mouth.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.100
Researchers linked the nitrate to nitrite conversion performed by these microbes

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.200
to the observed vascular response.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:12.760
Next up, most people assume the nutritional value of a meal is simply the sum of its individual

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:19.520
ingredients. In reality, the moment foods are combined enzymes and reactive compounds from one

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.100
item can alter compounds in another before they ever reach the intestine.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:30.600
Right now, as you consider your next smoothie, polyphenol oxidase from a banana is already

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:36.060
converting flavonols from berries into forms the body of sorbs far less efficiently.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.120
Adding bananas to berry smoothies sharply lowers the amount of flavonols that reach the bloodstream.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.660
The effect stems from polyphenol oxidase in the banana, reacting with the berry compounds during

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:54.420
blending. Researchers measured the reduction in human volunteers after controlled test drinks.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:59.420
The study shows that everyday food pairings can alter nutrient bioevalivity.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.480
A single blending step can cut circulating flavonol levels by more than half compared with berries

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:11.740
alone. The practical takeaway is to keep high oxidase fruits separate from polyphenol rich

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:18.300
ingredients, if maximizing those specific compounds is the goal. Future nutrition labels may

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:25.280
eventually list interaction warnings alongside standard nutrient values. From molecular interactions

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:32.160
in food to molecular interactions that shape pain circuits, mice given one dose of psilocybin

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.100
exhibited reduced neuropathic pain behaviors that lasted up to a month. The compound also

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:44.780
potentiated the effect of a standard analgesic. Imaging showed reorganization of pain processing

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:50.780
circuits in the brain. The study points to a non-opioid route for chronic pain management that

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:56.540
warrants further investigation. From brain circuit changes to another low-tech intervention that

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:02.840
supports mental and social health. University of Plymouth investigators reviewed evidence on tabletop

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:09.180
and role-playing games. Participants consistently reported higher engagement, stronger feelings of

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:15.260
inclusion and lower stress after regular play sessions. The benefits appear across age groups and

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.040
skill levels. The study concludes that structured play supports both cognitive and emotional health

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:27.400
outcomes. From human social play to the vast unknown social and biological systems still being

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:33.860
mapped in the deep ocean. Researchers formally described a golf ball-sized blue octopus found at

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:40.200
nearly 6,000 feet near an underwater mountain in the Galapagos. The animal was observed crawling

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:46.320
across the seafloor during a deep sea expedition and differed enough in morphology to warrant recognition

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:52.360
as a distinct species. The discovery highlights how little is known about life in the deep ocean around

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:59.220
the islands. The work appears in the journal Zutaksa. Further expeditions are planned to map additional

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:05.780
deep habitats in the region. Osaka Metropolitan University engineers developed a light-driven optical

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:12.460
fiber that gathers thousands of bacteria into a single microscopic spot. The technique shortens the

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:18.780
time needed to reach detectable thresholds in diagnostic samples. Early tests demonstrated improved

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.580
sensitivity for bacterial identification. The method is described in communications physics.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:31.560
Marine algae exposed to microplastic particles show reduced photosynthesis and slower population

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:37.880
growth. Researchers quantified the resulting drop in the ocean's capacity to sequester atmospheric

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:44.560
carbon dioxide. The calculation incorporates both direct toxicity and indirect effects on the marine

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:51.820
food web. The work provides a new term for global carbon cycle models. Spectroscopic observations

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:57.000
revealed methane in the atmosphere of a planet whose equilibrium temperature matches Earth's.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:03.420
The data added new constraint on models of how atmospheres form and evolve around planets of this size.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:09.300
Astronomers note the finding may refine understanding of Earth's own atmospheric chemistry.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:17.080
Additional observations are scheduled with larger telescopes. Researchers process more than 400,000

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:23.880
posts mentioning GLP-1 receptor agonists. The scan identified clusters of discussion around

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:29.300
menstrual irregularities, chills, and hot flashes that had not appeared prominently in trial data.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.560
The authors proposed social media mining as an adjunct for post marketing safety surveillance.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:42.020
Validation against electronic health records is underway. A survey spanning 30 countries found

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:48.040
that both election winners and losers continued to endorse majority rule and minority protections.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:53.260
Winning voters showed little appetite for retaliatory policies against opponents.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:59.740
The results indicate that effective polarization has not yet translated into rejection of democratic

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:06.720
procedures. Data were collected after recent national contests. Historical tracking data reveal that

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:12.780
periods of elevated solar activity correlate with faster orbital decay of low-Earth orbit objects.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:18.020
Increased atmosphere drag during solar maxima shortens satellite lifetimes.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:23.120
The relationship supplies a predictive variable for space traffic management models.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.420
Operators are incorporating the findings into reentry forecasts.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:34.160
Evaluations of current AI scientists platforms show they excel at narrow data-rich tasks

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.280
yet struggle when required to integrate distant facts across disciplines.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:45.460
The shortfall appears when problems demand both deep specialization and broad analogical leaps.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:51.200
Developers are now testing hybrid architectures that combine multiple reasoning strategies.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.040
Progress will be measured against benchmark problems drawn from recent discoveries.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.620
Keep an eye on additional deep sea expeditions planned around the Galapagos.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:05.820
That covers today's science and health news. Share this with someone who's curious about the latest

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:12.680
research. I'm Patrick and Vancouver. See you next time. This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.720
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
